From 6ffa41c8f70dff14042385f7e64c7d886996b4a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sagar Cheluvegowda <scheluve@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Apr 2026 12:19:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 20/28] PENDING: net: stmmac: qcom-ethqos: configure VDMA and
 PDMA channel mappings via device tree
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Currently, the Hardware DMA (HDMA) channel mappings for both TX and RX are
hardcoded in the qcom-ethqos driver. This limits the flexibility to
support different mapping requirements across various platforms.

This patch makes the HDMA channel mappings fully configurable
by introducing separate mappings for VDMA (Virtual DMA) and
PDMA (Physical DMA). Specifically, this patch:

1. Modifies `qcom_ethqos_hdma_cfg()` to dynamically parse the
separate VDMA and PDMA channel mappings from the device tree
using the `qcom,tx-pdma-map`, `qcom,rx-pdma-map`,
`qcom,tx-vdma-map`, and `qcom,rx-vdma-map` properties.
2. Ensures these parsed, separate mappings are correctly
utilized during DMA initialization to establish the proper
physical-to-virtual channel relationships.
3.  Updates `dwxgmac2_config_cbs()` in the core driver to handle
HDMA accurately. When HDMA is enabled, Credit Based Shaper (CBS)
parameters are managed at the Traffic Class (TC) level rather
than per MTL queue. This patch updates the function to utilize
the proper physical DMA (PDMA) mapping—which corresponds to the
correct TC—instead of the queue index. By routing the configuration
through the mapped PDMA channel, we ensure that the correct TC
is selected and the CBS parameters are accurately programmed for
the underlying hardware queues.

Change-Id: I559137afaafee8166a613d77fa8b2edec46ea0e3
Signed-off-by: Sagar Cheluvegowda <scheluve@qti.qualcomm.com>
